\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Begin, my soul, some heavenly theme;
\par Awake, my voice, and sing
\par The mighty works, or mightier name,
\par Of our eternal King.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Tell of His wondrous faithfulness,
\par And sound His power abroad;
\par Sing the sweet promise of Hos grace,
\par The quickening  word of God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Proclaim salvation from the Lord, 
\par For wretched, dying men:
\par His hand hath writ the sacred word
\par With an immortal pen.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Engraved as in eternal brass,
\par The mighty promise shines;
\par Nor can the powers of darkness raise
\par Those everlasting lines.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. His every word of grace is strong
\par As that which built the skies;
\par The voice that rolls the stars along
\par Speaks all the promises.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Now shall my fainting heart rejoice
\par To know Thy favour sure:
\par I trust the all-creating voice,
\par And faith desires no more.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

